{ h: "Gross profit vs net profit",
  body: "<p><strong>Gross profit</strong> = Net Sales − Cost of Goods Sold, where Cost of Goods Sold = Opening Stock + Net Purchases + Direct Expenses (carriage inwards, wages) − Closing Stock. It measures pure trading efficiency. <strong>Net profit</strong> then adds indirect incomes (commission received, discount received) and subtracts indirect expenses (salaries, rent, depreciation, bad debts). Net profit is transferred to the <strong>Capital Account</strong> (credit side — it increases the owner's claim), while drawings are deducted from capital. Remember: the balance sheet is <em>not</em> an account — it is a statement, and it must balance.</p>" }
